00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.200
Leah: There are many source code
control solutions available today, and

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.990
it can become a little overwhelming
when deciding which one is appropriate.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.549
Some are open source and have a large
supporting community of developers such as Git.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:17.260
and others are more business centred,
focusing on larger teams and specific software

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.750
such as Microsoft Team Foundation Server.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.300
Chris: Having the right system is important,
so there are key considerations that need to be

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.459
made when choosing a source control, such as:

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.340
• which programming languages it supports.

00:00:31.799 --> 00:00:37.289
• the popularity – this is a consideration as
a popular solution such as Git has a large

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:42.720
community which could be useful if support
is needed, but also if a product is popular,

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:45.129
it is more likely to be kept up to date.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:50.490
• Leah: is it fit for purpose – does it do
what it needs to do for a given project?

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:55.170
• what tools and features it includes – does
it have the necessary tools needed?

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:59.050
For example, does it have
a graphical user interface?

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.280
Or does it include a bug tracking system?

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:05.320
• Chris: ease of use – how
easy is it to learn and use?

00:01:05.639 --> 00:01:06.760
Is it intuitive?

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:11.660
For example, GitHub is easier to
use than its counterpart Git, due

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:13.570
to its graphical user interface.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:18.040
• hosting capabilities – is
it a cloud-based solution?

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.350
Is it open-source?

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:23.649
How much storage is available
for free and paid packages?

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:29.239
This is quite a serious consideration as
security and maintenance would also be a factor.

00:01:29.949 --> 00:01:34.870
Some companies would choose to have their source
code solution on their own servers, but there are

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:41.550
also more modern Cloud solutions which will also
offer built in security such as Azure DevOps.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:47.650
Leah: So, let’s have a look at some examples of
the more well-known source code control solutions.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:52.000
GitHub is one of the most popular
online cloud-based hosting version

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.130
control which is owned by Microsoft.

00:01:54.830 --> 00:02:00.610
It provides the distributed version control
of Git plus ‘access control’, ‘bug tracing’,

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.889
‘task management’, and ‘continuous integration’.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:09.859
It provides a desktop application which
has a graphical user interface, within

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:14.540
which Git commands can be run without
using the command line, so therefore

00:02:14.559 --> 00:02:16.969
simplifies the development workflow.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:22.479
As a free version it can be used for personal
projects with smaller storage capacity,

00:02:23.049 --> 00:02:27.310
but there is the option to upgrade to a
paid version which is more suitable for

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.739
companies with larger storage requirements.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:34.510
It can manage multiple projects and
has good documentation and support.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:39.589
Chris: Git is an open-source
distributed code control, that allows

00:02:39.609 --> 00:02:42.149
version control for a repository.

00:02:42.609 --> 00:02:47.079
It is good for intellectual software
applications, easy to learn and setup,

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:49.676
secure, and supports distributed versioning.

00:02:49.676 --> 00:02:50.014
Leah: Bitbucket Server is good for teams already
using ‘Atlassian’ products such as ‘Jira’.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:03:03.140
It suits team-based workspaces as well as
being a versioning solution, and it includes

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.579
project management, and collaboration.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:12.220
Whilst benefitting by having an intuitive GUI,
and being easy to learn, integration with external

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:15.889
systems such as a CMS, can be rather tricky.

00:03:16.779 --> 00:03:21.510
Chris: Team Foundation Server known as
Azure DevOps server is for teams that

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:26.060
use ‘Microsoft tools’ and is designed for
companies with its enterprise offerings.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.909
It integrates easily with existing
Microsoft IDEs such as Visual

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.400
Studio and project management tools.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.780
It can be expensive though and does
not have as much flexibility when

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.610
working with non-Microsoft tools.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.050
Leah: Don’t forget to check out our
website links to find out more information!

